    'Accessibility, autonomy, privacy, and trust',
    'Functional requirements and acceptance criteria',
    'Failure, recovery, and field-readiness test matrix',
    'Open design decisions and change-control rules',
    'Source lineage and design provenance'
],1):
    p=doc.add_paragraph(); p.paragraph_format.space_after=Pt(2); r=p.add_run(f'{idx:02d}  {title}'); r.font.size=Pt(10.5); r.bold=True if idx<=4 else False

add_callout('Reading rule', 'Treat named software, model, and hardware choices in historical source material as replaceable implementation detail unless this PRD explicitly promotes the underlying behavior to a product requirement. The durable object of this document is the operating philosophy, user experience, boundary model, and observable behavior.', 'F7F1E7','A9833F')
page_break()

# ---------- 1 ----------
doc.add_heading('1. Product Definition and Governing Principles', level=1)
add_label('PRD scope')
p=doc.add_paragraph('GrizOS is the GMRI / Workshop operating environment for shared work between biological and digital collaborators. This PRD defines only the user interface, spatial environment, and Dottie Hill operational intelligence surface. It does not define Project Sovereign internals.')

add_callout('Core distinction', 'GrizOS is not an intelligence and it is not a bag of tools. It is the operating environment that establishes boundaries, shared state, authority, context, and access to capabilities. Intelligences and tools participate through it; they do not become it.', 'EEF2F4','20364F')

doc.add_heading('1.1 Governing product principles', level=2)
principles=[
('P-01','Intent before application','The user should express what they are trying to accomplish before they are forced to choose an app, page, menu, or software silo.'),
('P-02','Technology adapts to the person','The system changes interaction density, modality, and presentation around the human rather than forcing the human to adapt to the system.'),
('P-03','Boundaries are explicit','Operating system, intelligence, tools, sensors, state, and authority remain distinguishable at runtime.'),
('P-04','Voice first; eyes up','Voice is the default intent channel. Visuals materialize when they add value. Touch is for precision. Typing is exceptional.'),
('P-05','World state outranks screen state','The persistent unit of truth is the shared world and its provenance, not whichever UI surface happens to be open.'),
('P-06','Local capability is real capability','Loss of connectivity must not collapse the Apple-side core into a nonfunctional shell.'),
('P-07','Uncertainty stays uncertainty','No subsystem silently promotes inference, ambiguity, or weak evidence to operational fact.'),
('P-08','Receipts are native','Material claims, actions, state changes, and Dottie judgments preserve provenance, confidence, and authority state.'),
('P-09','Attention is a protected resource','The system should metabolize complexity and interrupt only when consequence justifies interruption.'),
('P-10','Accessibility is architecture','Hands-busy, eyes-up, neurodivergent, mobility-limited, and one-hand/no-hand use are baseline design conditions, not later accommodations.'),
]
add_table(['ID','Principle','Product meaning'], principles, [0.55,1.7,4.35], 8.7)

doc.add_heading('1.2 Non-goals', level=2)
add_bullets([
    'Recreate a conventional desktop, browser, or phone UI inside 3D space.',
    'Use Dottie as the default renderer, router, or universal model for every interaction.',
    'Treat an immersive environment as a requirement for ResponderOS or CompanionOS.',
    'Make network access a prerequisite for basic orientation, navigation, local work, or device interaction.',
    'Hide state transitions, uncertainty, or authority boundaries to make the experience look smoother.',
    'Freeze current software-stack choices into the product definition.'
])

# ---------- 2 ----------
doc.add_heading('2. Product Family and Context Expressions', level=1)
add_fig(DIAG/'product_family.png','Figure 1. One capability philosophy, expressed through different mission contexts.',6.6)
p=doc.add_paragraph('GrizOS, ResponderOS, and CompanionOS are not ordered capability tiers. They share a broad capability substrate and diverge mainly by mission context, rationale, default logic, authority, and presentation. GrizOS remains the fullest GMRI expression because it also includes the immersive Workshop environment.')
add_table(['Expression','Primary context','Distinctive defaults','Economic / access doctrine'],[
('GrizOS','GMRI / Workshop; biological + digital collaboration','Full immersive spatial/VR environment; research and workshop context; broad capability exposure within GMRI authority','Internal GMRI operating environment'),
('ResponderOS','EMS when the responder is on duty','Responder doctrine, dispatch/agency context where applicable, high-consequence escalation logic; immersive Workshop not required','Core free for life to qualified users; possible future organization-funded clinical/institutional add-on'),
('CompanionOS','Disability, autonomy, and persistent situational awareness','Hands-busy/no-hands, eyes-up, independence, dignity, privacy; immersive Workshop not required','Core free for life to qualified users'),
], [1.0,1.65,2.9,1.15], 8.5)
add_callout('Product-family rule', 'Differences between the three expressions should be justified by context, logic, authority, or environment—not by artificially withholding core capability from one group.', 'F7F1E7','A9833F')

# ---------- 3 ----------
doc.add_heading('3. Boundary Architecture: OS, Intelligence, Tools, and Peers', level=1)
add_fig(DIAG/'boundary_model.png','Figure 2. Boundary model: intelligences and tools remain distinct from the operating environment.',6.7)
p=doc.add_paragraph('The operating system owns shared context, authority, state, routing, and capability exposure. An intelligence can reason, propose, request, converse, or collaborate. A tool can transform, retrieve, classify, render, sense, or act. The product must prevent category collapse: being intelligent does not make a component the operating system, and being useful does not make a tool a peer intelligence.')

doc.add_heading('3.1 Boundary requirements', level=2)
add_table(['ID','Requirement','Acceptance signal'],[
('BND-01','Every consequential action has an identifiable actor, authority source, tool/capability used, and resulting state change.','Audit view can answer “who/what did this, under what authority, and what changed?”'),
('BND-02','An intelligence cannot silently expand its own permissions by virtue of being the conversational front end.','Capability calls outside granted authority are refused or escalated.'),
('BND-03','Tool output remains attributable to the tool/source and is not silently rewritten into intelligence-owned fact.','Provenance survives presentation and summarization.'),
('BND-04','Digital collaborators may access the same operating environment as biological collaborators, subject to identity and authority.','A digital peer can inspect/manipulate permitted shared state without impersonating the OS.'),
('BND-05','Interface composition may be delegated to a lightweight interaction intelligence without making that intelligence authoritative for the underlying world state.','UI can be swapped without losing authoritative state or changing decision authority.'),
], [0.65,3.5,2.55], 8.6)

# ---------- 4 ----------
doc.add_heading('4. Interaction Model: Voice → Visual → Touch → Type', level=1)
add_fig(DIAG/'interaction_hierarchy.png','Figure 3. Interaction hierarchy and fallback order.',6.6)
add_callout('Locked interaction priority', 'Voice first. Visual second. Touch when needed. Typing hardly ever if avoidable.', 'E8F1F1','2D6F73')

doc.add_heading('4.1 Modality rules', level=2)
add_bullets([
    'Voice initiates most tasks, changes, queries, navigation intents, and tool requests.',
    'Visual output should be generated only when it improves orientation, comparison, manipulation, confirmation, or shared understanding.',
    'Touch is the preferred precision channel for selecting, confirming, moving, pinning, scrubbing, exploding, annotating, or disambiguating visual objects.',
    'Typing is retained for exact strings, code, identifiers, search terms, or environments where voice is inappropriate—not as the default route to capability.',
    'When speech recognition has meaningful ambiguity, the system asks rather than converting uncertainty into a fluent wrong action.',
    'Speech, visual, touch, haptic, and spatial cues should reinforce one another without requiring redundant user work.'
